import AxQM.Concrete.RotationDensity

/-!
# Concrete: iterating the Deutsch gate's target `iR_x(πα)` densely fills the `x`-rotations

## Mathematical content (the analytic core of Nielsen & Chuang, Exercise 4.44)

Exercise 4.44 asks to show that the three-qubit **Deutsch gate** `G = C²(iR_x(πα))` — the
doubly-controlled application of the single-qubit operation `iR_x(πα)` to the target — is universal
for quantum computation whenever `α` is *irrational*. Its analytic engine is the same one used for
Exercise 4.43 (`RotationDensity.lean`): iterating an irrational-angle rotation densely fills a
one-parameter rotation family. Here the iterated operation is the Deutsch target
`iRxMat θ = i · R_x(θ)` and the file establishes:

* `iRxMat_pow` — `(iR_x(θ))^k = iᵏ · R_x(kθ)`: iterating accumulates the phase as `iᵏ` and the
  angle as `kθ`.
* `iRxMat_pow_four` — `(iR_x(θ))^4 = R_x(4θ)`: every four iterations the global phase `i⁴ = 1`
  cancels, leaving a *phase-free* `x`-rotation. (At `α = 1`, `iR_x(π) = X`, so `G` is the Toffoli
  gate — the Deutsch gate is a continuous deformation of Toffoli.)
* `rotX_mem_closure_cyclic_iRx` — **the universality core**: when `α` is irrational, every
  `x`-rotation `R_x(β)` lies in the closure of the cyclic subgroup `⟨iR_x(πα)⟩` generated by the
  Deutsch target. Equivalently, iterating `G` (and its inverse) approximates an arbitrary
  `x`-rotation on the target to arbitrary accuracy — the density that (with the standard
  single-qubit-decomposition + controlled-gate assembly, §4.5) yields universality. For `α`
  rational this fails: `iR_x(πα)` then has finite order, so its subgroup is finite, not dense.
* `iRxMat_mem_unitaryGroup` / `iRxMat_pi` — the two bridges the *physics* gate needs: `iR_x(θ)` is
  unitary (a modulus-one scalar times a unitary), so it packages as an `Evolution`; and
  `iR_x(π) = X`, so the Deutsch gate is the Toffoli gate at `α = 1`. These feed
  `Postulates/API/DeutschGate.lean` (the gate `iRxGate`) and `NC/Ch4/Exercise4_44.lean`.

## Design notes

* **Why `α` irrational (not `¬∃r∈ℚ, α = r·2π`).** The density of `{R_x(n·4πα)}`
  requires `(4πα)/(2π) = 2α` to be irrational, i.e. `α` irrational — exactly the exercise's own
  hypothesis. The alternative "α not a rational multiple of `2π`" would admit `α = 1` (rational),
  where `G` is the Toffoli gate, which is *not* universal for quantum computation; so `Irrational α`
  is the faithful reading.
* **The cyclic subgroup in closed form.** `Matrix (Fin 2) (Fin 2) ℂ` is only a monoid, so the
  matrix `zpow` `(iR_x(πα))^n` for `n : ℤ` is not directly available. The subgroup `⟨iR_x(πα)⟩` is
  therefore written in the closed form `{iⁿ · R_x(nπα) : n ∈ ℤ}` (with `iⁿ` the `ℂ`-`zpow` and
  `R_x` total); `iRxMat_pow` records that its non-negative part `n ≥ 0` equals the genuine matrix
  powers. This mirrors the `ℤ`-subgroup (rather than `ℕ`-forward-orbit) reading chosen for
  Exercise 4.43 (`rotX_mem_closure_range_zsmul`), which is reused here directly at step `4πα`.
-/

namespace AxQM.Concrete

open Matrix Complex

/-- **Iterating `R_x` composes the angle** (the `x`-axis specialisation of `rotAxis_pow`):
`R_x(θ)^k = R_x(kθ)`. -/
theorem rotX_pow (θ : ℝ) (k : ℕ) : rotX θ ^ k = rotX (↑k * θ) :=
  rotAxis_pow ![1, 0, 0] θ k

/-- The **target operation of the Deutsch gate** `iR_x(θ) = i · R_x(θ)` as a raw `2 × 2` matrix
(Nielsen & Chuang, Exercise 4.44). The doubly-controlled application of this operation to the target
qubit is the Deutsch gate `G`. -/
noncomputable def iRxMat (θ : ℝ) : Matrix (Fin 2) (Fin 2) ℂ := Complex.I • rotX θ

/-- **Iterating `iR_x(θ)`** accumulates the phase as `iᵏ` and the angle as `kθ`:
`(iR_x(θ))^k = iᵏ · R_x(kθ)`. The scalar `i` factors through the power (`smul_pow`) and the
rotation angles add (`rotX_pow`). -/
theorem iRxMat_pow (θ : ℝ) (k : ℕ) : iRxMat θ ^ k = Complex.I ^ k • rotX (↑k * θ) := by
  rw [iRxMat, smul_pow, rotX_pow]

/-- **Four iterations of `iR_x(θ)` cancel the global phase:** `(iR_x(θ))^4 = R_x(4θ)`, since
`i⁴ = 1`. The phase `iᵏ` is `4`-periodic, so the phase-free iterates are exactly the multiples of
`4`; at `α = 1` this gives `(iR_x(π))^1 = X` (the Toffoli gate). -/
theorem iRxMat_pow_four (θ : ℝ) : iRxMat θ ^ 4 = rotX (4 * θ) := by
  rw [iRxMat_pow, Complex.I_pow_four, one_smul]
  norm_num

/-- **Universality core of the Deutsch gate (Nielsen & Chuang, Exercise 4.44).** When `α` is
irrational, iterating the Deutsch target operation `iR_x(πα)` densely fills all `x`-rotations: every
`R_x(β)` lies in the closure of the cyclic subgroup `⟨iR_x(πα)⟩ = {iⁿ · R_x(nπα) : n ∈ ℤ}`.

Because `i⁴ = 1`, the phase-free iterates are `(iR_x(πα))^{4k} = R_x(4kπα) = R_x(k · 4πα)`, i.e. the
cyclic subgroup of `x`-rotations generated by `R_x(4πα)`. Since `(4πα)/(2π) = 2α` is irrational
(as `α` is), Exercise 4.43's `rotX_mem_closure_range_zsmul` gives that these already approximate
every `R_x(β)`; they form a subset of `⟨iR_x(πα)⟩`, so `closure_mono` transfers the density. -/
theorem rotX_mem_closure_cyclic_iRx {α : ℝ} (hα : Irrational α) (β : ℝ) :
    rotX β ∈ closure (Set.range fun n : ℤ => Complex.I ^ n • rotX (n • (Real.pi * α))) := by
  have h2 : Irrational (2 * α) := by simpa using hα.natCast_mul (m := 2) (by norm_num)
  have hθ : Irrational ((4 * Real.pi * α) / (2 * Real.pi)) := by
    rw [show (4 * Real.pi * α) / (2 * Real.pi) = 2 * α by
          rw [div_eq_iff (by positivity : (0 : ℝ) < 2 * Real.pi).ne']; ring]
    exact h2
  refine closure_mono ?_ (rotX_mem_closure_range_zsmul hθ β)
  rintro _ ⟨k, rfl⟩
  refine ⟨4 * k, ?_⟩
  simp only [_root_.zpow_mul, show (4 : ℤ) = ((4 : ℕ) : ℤ) from rfl, zpow_natCast,
    Complex.I_pow_four, _root_.one_zpow, one_smul]
  congr 1
  push_cast [zsmul_eq_mul]; ring

/-- **The `i`-coset of the Deutsch orbit is dense in the phased `x`-rotations** (Nielsen & Chuang,
Exercise 4.44). When `α` is irrational, every phased `x`-rotation `i · R_x(β)` lies in the closure
of the cyclic subgroup `⟨iR_x(πα)⟩ = {iⁿ · R_x(nπα) : n ∈ ℤ}`. This is the `iⁿ = i` (i.e.
`n ≡ 1 (mod 4)`) coset of the orbit: the iterates `(iR_x(πα))^{4k+1} = i · R_x((4k+1)πα)` accumulate
the phase `i`, and since `{4kπα}` is dense (as `2α` is irrational, `rotX_mem_closure_cyclic_iRx`)
they approximate `i · R_x(β)` for every `β`.

Two Deutsch-gate facts are its immediate consequences: the phase `i · I` at `β = 0`
(`iScalar_mem_closure_cyclic_iRx`, which lifts to the phase gate `S`), and the Pauli `X` at `β = π`
(`pauliX_mem_closure_cyclic_iRx`, `i · R_x(π) = X`, which lifts to `CNOT`/`Toffoli`).

Proved by transporting `rotX_mem_closure_cyclic_iRx` at angle `β - πα` through the continuous map
`M ↦ i · (R_x(πα) · M)`, which sends the orbit into itself (`i · (R_x(πα) · (iⁿ R_x(nπα))) =
i^{n+1} R_x((n+1)πα)`) and sends `R_x(β - πα)` to `i · (R_x(πα) · R_x(β - πα)) = i · R_x(β)`. -/
theorem iScaledRotX_mem_closure_cyclic_iRx {α : ℝ} (hα : Irrational α) (β : ℝ) :
    Complex.I • rotX β
      ∈ closure (Set.range fun n : ℤ => Complex.I ^ n • rotX (n • (Real.pi * α))) := by
  set f : ℤ → Matrix (Fin 2) (Fin 2) ℂ := fun n => Complex.I ^ n • rotX (n • (Real.pi * α)) with hf
  have hg : Continuous fun M : Matrix (Fin 2) (Fin 2) ℂ =>
      Complex.I • (rotX (Real.pi * α) * M) := by
    fun_prop
  have himg : (fun M : Matrix (Fin 2) (Fin 2) ℂ => Complex.I • (rotX (Real.pi * α) * M)) ''
      Set.range f ⊆ Set.range f := by
    rintro _ ⟨_, ⟨n, rfl⟩, rfl⟩
    refine ⟨n + 1, ?_⟩
    simp only [hf]
    rw [mul_smul_comm, rotX_mul_rotX, smul_smul]
    congr 1
    · rw [zpow_add_one₀ Complex.I_ne_zero, mul_comm]
    · congr 1; push_cast [zsmul_eq_mul]; ring
  have hmem := image_closure_subset_closure_image hg
    (Set.mem_image_of_mem _ (rotX_mem_closure_cyclic_iRx hα (β - Real.pi * α)))
  have hval : Complex.I • (rotX (Real.pi * α) * rotX (β - Real.pi * α))
      = Complex.I • rotX β := by
    rw [rotX_mul_rotX, show Real.pi * α + (β - Real.pi * α) = β by ring]
  rw [hval] at hmem
  exact closure_mono himg hmem

/-- **The phase `i·I` is a closure limit of the Deutsch orbit** (Nielsen & Chuang, Exercise 4.44).
When `α` is irrational, the scalar operator `i · I` lies in the closure of the cyclic subgroup
`⟨iR_x(πα)⟩ = {iⁿ · R_x(nπα) : n ∈ ℤ}`: it is the `β = 0` case of
`iScaledRotX_mem_closure_cyclic_iRx` (`i · R_x(0) = i · I`).

Physically this is what lets the *once*-controlled Deutsch gate reach the **phase gate** `S`: the
controlled application of `i · I` to the target is `S ⊗ I` (the accumulated `i` becomes a relative
phase on the control), so the reachability of `i · I` here lifts to the reachability of `S`
(`Postulates/API/DeutschGatePhaseGate.lean`). -/
theorem iScalar_mem_closure_cyclic_iRx {α : ℝ} (hα : Irrational α) :
    Complex.I • (1 : Matrix (Fin 2) (Fin 2) ℂ)
      ∈ closure (Set.range fun n : ℤ => Complex.I ^ n • rotX (n • (Real.pi * α))) := by
  have h := iScaledRotX_mem_closure_cyclic_iRx hα 0
  rwa [show rotX (0 : ℝ) = 1 from rotAxis_zero _] at h

/-- **`iR_x(θ)` is unitary.** The Deutsch target `iRxMat θ = i · R_x(θ)` is a modulus-one scalar
`i` times the unitary `R_x(θ)`, hence unitary:
`(i • R_x θ) · star (i • R_x θ) = (i · ī) • (R_x · R_xᴴ) = 1 • 1 = 1` (`i · ī = |i|² = 1`). This is
the `Evolution` proof obligation for the physics gate `iRxGate`. -/
theorem iRxMat_mem_unitaryGroup (θ : ℝ) : iRxMat θ ∈ Matrix.unitaryGroup (Fin 2) ℂ := by
  rw [Matrix.mem_unitaryGroup_iff, iRxMat, star_smul, smul_mul_smul_comm,
    Matrix.mem_unitaryGroup_iff.mp (rotX_mem_unitaryGroup θ),
    show Complex.I * star Complex.I = 1 by simp [Complex.I_mul_I], one_smul]

/-- **At `θ = π` the Deutsch target is the Pauli `X`:** `iR_x(π) = X`. Since
`R_x(π) = -iX` (`cos(π/2) = 0`, `sin(π/2) = 1`), the phase `i` cancels the `-i`: `i · (-iX) = X`.
This is why the Deutsch gate `G = C²(iR_x(πα))` becomes the Toffoli gate `C²(X)` at `α = 1`. -/
theorem iRxMat_pi : iRxMat Real.pi = pauliX := by
  rw [iRxMat, rotX_eq, pauliX]
  ext i j
  fin_cases i <;> fin_cases j <;>
    simp [Matrix.smul_apply, Real.cos_pi_div_two, Real.sin_pi_div_two]

/-- **The Pauli `X` is a closure limit of the Deutsch orbit** (Nielsen & Chuang, Exercise 4.44).
When `α` is irrational, the Pauli matrix `X` lies in the closure of the cyclic subgroup
`⟨iR_x(πα)⟩ = {iⁿ · R_x(nπα) : n ∈ ℤ}`. This is the `β = π` case of
`iScaledRotX_mem_closure_cyclic_iRx`: `X = i · R_x(π)` (`iRxMat_pi`, since `R_x(π) = -iX`), the
`iⁿ = i` coset of the orbit at angle `π`.

Physically this is what lets the Deutsch gate reach the reversible gates `CNOT = C(X)` and
`Toffoli = C²(X)`: `X` is densely reachable on the target, so the once- and doubly-controlled
embeddings send it to `CNOT`/`Toffoli` (`Postulates/API/DeutschGateReversible.lean`). Note the gate
`iR_x(πα)` itself equals `X` only at the *rational* value `α = 1` (`iRxMat_pi`); for irrational `α`,
`X` is reached only in the limit. -/
theorem pauliX_mem_closure_cyclic_iRx {α : ℝ} (hα : Irrational α) :
    pauliX ∈ closure (Set.range fun n : ℤ => Complex.I ^ n • rotX (n • (Real.pi * α))) := by
  rw [← iRxMat_pi, iRxMat]
  exact iScaledRotX_mem_closure_cyclic_iRx hα Real.pi

end AxQM.Concrete
